# Slow gate — the two unit suites, plus a typecheck the pre-commit hook may
# never have run (a `--no-verify` commit, a commit made by another tool, a
# rebase). Nothing reaches the remote without passing what CI is about to run.
#
# Measured on a Windows dev machine: typecheck ~17s, `@ticket/api` ~28s,
# `@ticket/web` ~4min — the web suite is jsdom-bound and Windows is ~4x slower
# than ubuntu-latest here (see docs/standards/testing.md). That total is why
# this is per-push and not per-commit: a five-minute pre-commit is one people
# learn to `--no-verify` around, which costs more than it saves.
#
# E2E is not here on purpose. It needs a Postgres, a migrated ticket_manager_test
# and two servers on alt ports (SCRIPTS.md); CI's `e2e` job owns it.
bun run typecheck
bun run test
